      "id": "jguzymz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Nature of Solar Radiation"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Insolation is incoming shortwave solar radiation received at the Earth's surface.",
        "The Earth maintains a constant temperature by balancing incoming shortwave solar radiation with outgoing longwave terrestrial radiation.",
        "Albedo measures surface reflectivity; fresh snow reflects the highest amount of solar radiation.",
        "Subtropical deserts receive the highest amount of insolation due to low cloud cover, rather than the equator.",
        "Temperature inversion happens when warm air overlies cold air near the surface, reversing the normal lapse rate."
      ],
      "id": "11bimp3"
    },
