    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Normal Lapse Rate equals a drop of 6.5°C per 1,000 meters (or 1°C per 165 meters) rise in altitude in the troposphere.",
        "Temperature Inversion requires specific conditions: long winter nights, clear skies, still/calm air, and dry air near the snow-covered ground.",
        "Isotherms bend significantly towards the equator over oceans in summer and towards the poles over land in winter."
      ],
